.TH CYAML_NODE_TAG 3 "2026-08-17" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_node_tag \- return a node's YAML tag
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

const char *cyaml_node_tag(cyaml node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Return the YAML tag of node, or NULL when node carries no tag.

A node that the parser reads from a document with an explicit tag
carries the fully resolved tag string here, whether the document wrote
it as "!!str", a custom "!foo", a shorthand that %TAG resolves, or a
verbatim tag.  The tag is one of the seven CYAML_TAG_* constants
(CYAML_TAG_NULL, _BOOL, _INT, _FLOAT, _STR, _SEQ, _MAP) or a custom tag
string.  A node with no tag returns NULL, and this includes a node
whose type comes only from implicit core-schema resolution.

A dictionary key can never carry a tag, because the keys of this DOM
are plain strings, not nodes (see cyaml_dictionary_get(3)).  A tag on a
key in the document types that key exactly as it types a value, and the
dictionary stores the canonical text of the typed key; there is no
place to store the tag itself.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
node  DOM node handle.  It can be NULL, in which case the function
      returns NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A borrowed, non-owning tag string, or NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_node_set_tag (3),
.BR cyaml_type (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_get (3)
